Subject: Do not reopen the pty by name where TIOCSCTTY made it the controlling tty
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Werewolf runs sshd without CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE]
Reference: werewolf docs/design/ssh-hardening.md

pty_make_controlling_tty opens the pty by name and closes it again, as root,
after pty_setowner gave it to the logged-in user. Where TIOCSCTTY exists, the
ioctl has already made it the controlling tty, and the /dev/tty open that
follows checks it. Without CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE the redundant open fails for every
user but root and logs "/dev/pts/N: Permission denied" at error level.

diff --git a/sshpty.c b/sshpty.c
--- a/sshpty.c
+++ b/sshpty.c
@@ -123,11 +123,13 @@
 	if (setpgrp(0,0) < 0)
 		error("SETPGRP %s",strerror(errno));
 #endif /* NEED_SETPGRP */
+#ifndef TIOCSCTTY
 	fd = open(tty, O_RDWR);
 	if (fd == -1)
 		error("%.100s: %.100s", tty, strerror(errno));
 	else
 		close(fd);
+#endif /* !TIOCSCTTY */
 
 	/* Verify that we now have a controlling tty. */
 	fd = open(_PATH_TTY, O_WRONLY);
